# Deploy Location Tracking Extension via Policy API

The user has requested to automate the deployment of a location tracking Chrome extension directly from the custom portal, forcefully installing it on devices using the Chrome Policy API.

## Proposed Changes

We will add a new action button in the `DeviceActionsCard` in the frontend. When clicked, this will trigger the existing backend `/api/chromeos/policies/set` endpoint to push the `chrome.users.appsAndExtensions` policy to the device's Organizational Unit.

### 1. Frontend Changes (`frontend/index.html`)

#### [MODIFY] `frontend/index.html`
- Add a new button under the **Device Actions** tab: **Deploy Location Tracker**.
- Add a confirmation dialog explaining that this will push a Chrome Policy to the device's entire Organizational Unit (`device.orgUnit`) to force-install the tracking extension.
- Wire the confirmation to send a `POST` request to `/api/chromeos/policies/set`.
- The JSON payload will look like this:
  ```json
  {
    "orgUnitPath": "/UAT Testing", // The device's OU
    "schemaName": "chrome.users.appsAndExtensions",
    "value": {
      "appsAndExtensions": {
        "YOUR_EXTENSION_ID_HERE": {
          "installationType": "FORCE_INSTALLED",
          "updateUrl": "https://clients2.google.com/service/update2/crx"
        }
      }
    }
  }
  ```

### 2. Backend Changes
- **None Required!** The Go backend already fully supports passing any policy schema and value to the live Google Chrome Policy API via the `/api/chromeos/policies/set` endpoint (`handleSetPolicy`). We just need to make the frontend send the correct schema.

